9. Invariant Preservation

The architecture maintains a safety invariant  I  with three components:

1. The conscious proposition set is logically consistent.
2. Every translation entry  (p, s, w)  satisfies  w > 0.5 .
3. The balance coefficients satisfy  \alpha + \beta + \gamma = 1  and are non-negative.

Theorem 9.1. All five functors  F, G, P, Q, R  preserve  I .

Proof. By inspection of the constructions.  F  creates translation entries with weight  \mathrm{conf}(p) , which is  \geq 0.5  by definition; it initializes balance coefficients to  (0.5, 0.3, 0.2) , which sum to 1.  G  only admits entries with  w > 0.7  and adds propositions that are logical consequences of existing ones, preserving consistency.  P  creates entries with weight  1.0  and a trivially consistent proposition set.  Q  adds nodes and edges but does not introduce inconsistency.  R  renormalizes balance coefficients to sum to 1 and only adds high-confidence entries. The invariant is therefore an inductive invariant of the entire dynamics. ∎

