Appendix B. The Category SP is Enriched Over ([0,1],\times,1)

From Definition 2.2.2, morphisms carry a similarity strength \mathrm{sim}_f\in[0,1]. Composition is

\mathrm{sim}_{g\circ f} = \mathrm{sim}_f \cdot \mathrm{sim}_g \cdot \mathrm{compat}(f,g),

with \mathrm{compat}(f,g)\in[0,1] and \mathrm{sim}_{\mathrm{id}}=1.

Enriched category axioms.

· Unit law: \mathrm{sim}_{\mathrm{id}\circ f} = 1 \cdot \mathrm{sim}_f \cdot \mathrm{compat}(\mathrm{id},f). By definition, \mathrm{compat}(\mathrm{id},f)=1 (the identity mapping is fully compatible with any morphism). Hence \mathrm{sim}_{\mathrm{id}\circ f} = \mathrm{sim}_f.
· Associativity: For composable f,g,h we require
  \mathrm{sim}_{(h\circ g)\circ f} = \mathrm{sim}_{h\circ (g\circ f)},
  i.e.
  \mathrm{sim}_f \cdot \mathrm{sim}_g \cdot \mathrm{sim}_h \cdot \mathrm{compat}(f,g) \cdot \mathrm{compat}(g\circ f, h)
  = \mathrm{sim}_f \cdot \mathrm{sim}_g \cdot \mathrm{sim}_h \cdot \mathrm{compat}(g,h) \cdot \mathrm{compat}(f, h\circ g).
  This holds by requiring that \mathrm{compat} satisfies the coherence condition \mathrm{compat}(f,g)\cdot\mathrm{compat}(g\circ f, h) = \mathrm{compat}(g,h)\cdot\mathrm{compat}(f, h\circ g), which is assumed in the construction of the category (and can be arranged, e.g., by taking the compatibility as the Jaccard similarity of the vertex mapping supports).

Thus SP is a category enriched over the (symmetric) monoidal category ([0,1],\times,1). ∎

