Notes on the Bibliography

All references listed above have been verified through internet searches to confirm authorship, title, journal or publisher, year of publication, and, where available, DOI or other persistent identifier. The bibliography is organized by thematic area to reflect the interdisciplinary nature of the Mii Logical Architecture, which draws upon category theory, cognitive science, consciousness studies, domain theory, stochastic approximation, evolutionary computation, sheaf theory, and neurosymbolic AI. The foundational texts by Mac Lane, Borceux, Lawvere & Schanuel, Awodey, Fong & Spivak, Mac Lane & Moerdijk, and Kashiwara & Schapira provide the mathematical backbone; the works by Phillips, Wilson, Tsuchiya, Saigo, Prentner, and Kleiner constitute the emerging field of categorical cognitive science; the papers by Gavranović et al., Romero Schellhorn & Mossakowski, van Krieken et al., and Alpay represent recent advances in categorical AI architectures; and the remaining entries cover the supporting theoretical machinery (fixed points, learning algorithms, sheaf semantics) that underpins the formal results proved in the dissertation.
